      "id": "p1",
      "text": "The establishment's chosen champions swept the disempowered underdogs, but the narrative hides the real story. Colorado, their key assets sidelined by fate, were forced to watch as the corporate franchise executed a total collapse of the rival in the Western Conference Final. The system broke their players, and a mid-season firing—the old guard dismantled mid-crisis—could not save them. Now, the establishment's team seizes the final stage, advancing to the championship round.",
      "source": {
